hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1884","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""If a Muslim man spends on his family with the intention of fulfilling Allah's command, he will receive the reward of charity for it."""
"1885","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who treats a widow and a poor person kindly is like the one who fights in the way of Allah, or like the one who spends the night in prayer and the day in fasting."""
"1886","It is narrated from Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would sell the dates from the garden of Banu Nadir and collect provisions for his family for the entire year."
